    "full_details": "Notices\nThe \"Ring Production Campaign\" is here! Production costs halved and battle rewards increased!\nCampaign\n2026-04-15 17:00:00\n（JST/GMT+9）\n\"Ring Production Campaign\" is here.\nDuring the campaign, the costs of producing \"rings\" and \"Ring Gemstone+\" are\nhalved\n!\nPlus, you'll\nreceive more\n\"Ring Gemstones\" than usual from the \"LafCof Phantoms & the Ring Gem Temple\" battle rewards!\nUse this chance to produce lots of rings!\nCampaign Duration\nStarts after the April 15, 2026 (Wed) maintenance and ends before the April 30, 2026 (Thu) maintenance.\nRing\nA Ring is a piece of equipment that is different from armor.\nUnlock Ring by completing the main quest on 50F of Aincrad.\nThis item can be produced, and it provides a Main Effect that increases natural Element damage, as well as up to two types of Random Bonuses, such as increased attack.\nBy equipping a ring, you will also be able to equip an Ability Skill Record as an EX Ability.\nUp to two rings can be equipped, and an EX Ability can be equipped to each.\nKoharu can also equip rings and EX Abilities. Assisting Characters cannot equip them.\nEffect Examples\nItem Name\nMain Effect\nRandom Bonus\nItem Icon\nFire Ring I\nFire element damage +1.5%.\nAttack +1.5%.\nDamage done to enemies weak to slashing +1.5%.\nWater Ring II\nWater element damage +2.5%.\nCritical rate +5%.\nDamage done to enemies weak to thrusting +2.5%.\nWind Ring III\nWind element damage +5%.\nPoison resistance +10%.\nDamage done to enemies weak to blunt +5%.\nRing Production\nIt can be produced using materials such as the Ring Gemstone obtained in \"LafCof Phantoms & the Ring Gem Temple\", and \"Coarse Stones\" dropped on each floor.\nYou can use a Ring as a material to produce a higher-rarity Ring.\nProduce lots of rings until you have one with your favorite effects and bonuses.\nIncreased Ring Gemstone Battle Rewards\nCleared Wave\nNormal Amount\nIncreased Amount\n5\n8\n10\n10\n8\n10\n15\n10\n15\n20\n10\n15\n25\n10\n20\n30\n10\n25\n35\n10\n30\n40\n10\n35\n45\n12\n40\n50\n12\n45\nEvery 5 waves thereafter\n10\n50\nSee here for more details on the \"Ring\"\nSee here for more details on the \"LafCof Phantoms & the Ring Gem Temple\"\nImportant\nThe schedule may be subject to change without notice. Thank you for your understanding.\nGo to Notice List",
    "startTime": "2026-04-14T19:00:00+00:00",
