    "full_details": "Notices\nA challenge from the game's management team! Extremely Difficult \"Fatal Battle: Strict Hermit\"!\nEVENT\n2024-12-28 12:00:00\n（JST/GMT+9）\nA challenge from the game's management team!\nExtremely difficult! The devs invite you to rise to the challenge!\nThe extremely difficult dungeon \"Fatal Battle\" has appeared!\nLet's make full use of our abilities and challenge it with all we've got!\nRewards\nThere are two dungeons available: Fatal Battle Super and Fatal Battle Super (Group OK).\nIf you defeat the boss of \"Fatal Battle Super\", you will receive the \"\nF.S. Crab Victor S\n\" item as proof and the \"F.S. Crab Victor S\" record from the achievements.\nDefeat the \"Fatal Battle Super (Group OK)\" boss and receive the \"\nF.S. Crab Opponent S\n\" item as well as the \"F.S. Crab Opponent S\" record from the achievements as proof of defeating a powerful enemy.\nDungeon\nRecord\nAchievement Requirements\nAchievement Rewards\nFatal Battle Super\nF.S. Crab Victor S\nObtain the F.S. Crab Victor S\nRevive Crystal×1\nFatal Battle Super (Group OK)\nF.S. Crab Opponent S\nObtain the F.S. Crab Opponent S\nRevive Crystal×1\nF.S. Crab Victor S Record Background\nF.S. Crab Opponent S Record Background\nHow to Participate\nTalk to the \"Fatal Battle\" NPC at the \"Teleport Gate Plaza\" to challenge it.\nEvent Period\nDecember 28, 2024 (Sat) 12:00 - January 5, 2025 (Sun) 23:59 (JST/UTC+9)\nParticipation Requirements\nComplete Main quest [The Indomitable Fang]\nBoss Monster\nFatal Strict Hermit\nDetails\nA total of four bosses will appear.\nEach boss is breakable.\n▼Fatal Träumerei Hermit\nAt the start of battle, it gains a stack buff that reduces damage.\n▼Fatal Plasterer Hermit\nIt deals Skill Breakable attacks, and can Skill Break with Blunt Element skills.\nThey have high damage resistance.\nYou can inflict large amounts of damage when a break happens.\n▼Fatal Strict Hermit Chaos\nIt deals Skill Breakable attacks, and can Skill Break with Dagger skills.\nThey have high damage resistance.\nDepending on the monster's status ailment (Poison,Burn, Bleed, Frostbite) stacks, the damage it takes increases.\n▼Fatal Strict Hermit\nIt deals Skill Breakable attacks, and can Skill Break with Thrust Element skills.\nThey have high damage resistance.\nThey are resistant to status ailments, but depending on the monster's status ailment (Poison,Burn, Bleed, Frostbite) stacks, the damage it takes increases.\nWhen a break or skill break happens, they will receive a stack debuffs that increase the damage they take.\nThis boss will use a variety of buffs, debuffs, and status ailments to lure the player to their death.\nDetermine the boss's state and the progress of the battle, and use your battle experience to defeat it.\nWeakness\n？？？\nResistance\n？？？\n* Break: Filling the entire Break Gauge will temporarily immobilize the boss and remove all of its buff effects.\n* Skill Break: By completely lowering the Skill Break Gauge, the boss will be temporarily immobilized and all of its buff effects will be removed.\nFor details on the effects of \"Status Ailments,\" please check in-game via \"Menu\" > \"System\" > \"Help\" > \"Buff, Debuff, and Status Ailments.\"\nAlternatively, please refer to the\n\"Status Ailments\"\nsection of the Play Guide.\n\"Groups\"\nYou can take on \"Fatal Battle Super (Group OK)\" with a group of up to 18 members.\nHow to Join Groups\nTo create or join a group, talk to the Fatal Battle NPC and select Fatal Battle Super (Group OK), then choose \"Challenge with a group (18)\".\nYou will automatically move to the standby map.\nYou can display the standby member list from the action button on the bottom right of the screen.\nWhen groups are formed, players who are not already in a party will be put into a party together and sent to the dungeon automatically.\nIf you would like to join a random group, we recommend using \"Quick Group\" to automatically join a group you can participate in.\nWhile on the Fatal Battle group Waiting Room screen, players can check the number of members, view the weapons equipped to Set 1, and see the Group Total Power.\nThe \"18\" on the button indicates the maximum number of group members.\nIf you are in a party, only the party leader can create or join a Group.\nScore Rewards\nFatal Battle Super\nTotal scores\nScore Rewards\nAmount\n1000\nRevive Crystal\n3\nFatal Battle Super (Group OK)\nTotal scores\nScore Rewards\nAmount\n1000\nRevive Crystal\n3\nChallenge Rewards\n·Fatal Battle Super\nChallenge Name\nPrimary Reward\nAmount\nDefeat all enemies\nF.S. Crab Victor S\n1\nCompleted without any tumble\nHealing Crystal\n1\nUsed switch 6 chain and above\nLife Potion\n1\n·Fatal Battle Super (Group OK)\nChallenge Name\nPrimary Reward\nAmount\nDefeat all enemies\nF.S. Crab Opponent S\n1\nCompleted without any tumble\nHealing Crystal\n1\nUsed switch 6 chain and above\nLife Potion\n1\nImportant\nThe same boss will appear in both \"Fatal Battle Super\" and \"Fatal Battle Super (Group OK)\" dungeons.\nYou can get the \"F.S. Crab Victor S\" and \"F.S. Crab Opponent S\" items from challenge rewards.\nThe \"F.S. Crab Victor S\" and \"F.S. Crab Opponent S\" items will be deleted on January 5, 2025 (Sun) 23:59 (JST/UTC+9).\nCan be attempted in a party of up to 6 players.\nThe schedule may be subject to change without notice. Thank you for your understanding.\nGo to Notice List",
    "startTime": "2024-12-28T03:00:00+00:00",
