    "full_details": "Notices\n[Aincrad Conquest Anniversary] An All-Out Battle against The Skull Reaper with increased rewards! \"Aincrad Conquest Anniversary: Battle in Edge of Hell's Abyss\" is here!\nEVENT\n2024-11-07 14:55:00\n（JST/GMT+9）\nAincrad Conquest Anniversary!\nThe Skull Reaper was the final floor boss defeated by the Assault Team in the original story of Sword Art Online.\nTo celebrate the date of its defeat, November 7, 2024, we are holding Aincrad Conquest Anniversary: Battle in Edge of Hell's Abyss, where you can once again take on The Skull Reaper!\nIn this event, the drop rate for \"\nCore Metal+++\n\" is greatly increased compared to regular All-Out Battles against The Skull Reaper, and you can also get many \"\nMemoria Niter S\n\" throughout the event!\nYou can also acquire a record exclusive to this event if you're able to earn a damage rank of S or better!\nHow to Participate\nTalk to \"Kirito\" at the \"Teleport Gate Plaza\" to challenge the dungeon.\nClear it as many times as necessary until the total HP reaches zero and they have been defeated.\n* There is a limit to the amount of HP that can be diminished in a single battle.\n\"The Skull Reaper\" will reappear after \"Defeat\".\nEvent Period\nNovember 7, 2024 (Thu) 14:55 - Before the November 13, 2024 (Wed) maintenance (JST/UTC+9).\nParticipation Requirements\nComplete the 75F Main Quest\nBoss Monster\nImportant\nPlease check all Rewards in the game.\nUp to 6 players can join the dungeon at one time.\nYou can still complete a dungeon if you run out of time, but you will not acquire items dropped by the undefeated monsters.\nIf you go to the title screen or are disconnected and do not return to the dungeon, you will not be counted as a remaining player, and you will not receive any Damage Points.\nIf all party members escape through the Exit, no Damage Points will be counted from the time of entry until the time of escape.\nDamage Points can be received when the result screen is displayed.\nThere are no First Attack or Last Attack bonus.\nThe schedule may be subject to change without notice. Thank you for your understanding.\nGo to Notice List",
    "startTime": "2024-11-07T05:55:00+00:00",
    "endTime": "2024-11-12T19:00:00+00:00"
